    35	#    The solver below removes these assumptions explicitly.
    36	# d) Placement legality:
    37	#    The generator paints the stripe background first, then reserves the 3x3
    38	#    destination block, then places ring barriers, then extends them outward.
    39	#    Maroons are only placed on stripe-floor cells, never on the destination or
    40	#    on wall/gate cells, so erasing a moved token always restores a well-defined
    41	#    visible background color.
    42	# e/f/g) Visual observability and anti-degeneration:
    43	#    The stripe pattern repeats across the whole board, so the two background
